==== OEM easy installation ====

Before setting up this router, do NOT connect it to the internet.  Prevent it from activating the TP-Link cloud feature.  Connect a cable using an ethernet LAN port to a computer with a ethernet port.  The default IP of the router will be http://192.168.0.1, a DHCP server is active by default.  If you have ever used your browser to setup this router once, there is a problem with a permanent redirect in the web GUI which will prevent you from login in with the correct password. (you will see a login loop using the correct password but no message that indicates a problem. When typing a wrong password it will show a popup box complaining).  The simple remedy is to flash your router in an anonymous browser window, which will not be subject to the permanent redirect problem.

You can install OpenWRT from the firmware that comes with the C6U. To do so, click on the ''Advanced tab'', choose ''System Tools'' from the left side menu, and pick ''Firmware Upgrade'' from the submenu options. In the main window, under ''Manual Upgrade'', click ''Browse''. Select the OpenWRT firmware file downloaded (see previous section). The filename may be of the form ''openwrt-21.02.1-ramips-mt7621-tplink_archer-c6u-v1-squashfs-factory.bin''. you do not need to rename the file.

In two of three test cases it was observed that the ''System Tools'' menu did not contain the ''Manual upload'' firmware section.  To enable this menu, After setting the admin password after first boot, you have to change the router ''Operation Mode'' in the menu.  Just select whatever mode that is not selected.  It will reboot the router and when you login again and navigate to the ''System Tools'' menu, you will see the ''Firmware Upgrade'' submenu now. In 1 test case, this problem did not happen.

If you happen to need to reset the router to it's defaults, keep the reset button pressed for 10 seconds and watch the LED behavior change, release and let it boot.  These routers reboot fast.

For configuring the router after installing OpenWrt, follow the [[docs:guide-user:base-system:start]] documentation

